    "en": {
      "summary": "Bipolar involves episodes of mania/hypomania and depression. NHS: specialist mental-health pathways; mood stabilisers are clinician-prescribed — never invent doses. Emergency: suicidal plans, psychosis with danger, or mania with no sleep and risky behaviour — crisis services / emergency care. See mental-health-crisis entry.",
